```

```sql
--Description: Build a prototype calculation for one cohort (09-Jul) to compute Week-2 retention;  
--this pattern will later be generalized for all cohorts.  
WITH
cohort_users AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT "user_pseudo_id"
    FROM FIREBASE.ANALYTICS_153293282."EVENTS_20180709"
    WHERE "event_name" = 'session_start'
),
week2_returners AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT "user_pseudo_id"
    FROM FIREBASE.ANALYTICS_153293282."EVENTS_20180723"
    WHERE "event_name" = 'session_start'
)
SELECT
    COUNT(*)                                  AS "cohort_size",
    SUM(CASE WHEN cu."user_pseudo_id" IN (SELECT "user_pseudo_id" FROM week2_returners) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) 
                                              AS "week2_returners"
FROM cohort_users cu;
```

These ten progressively more sophisticated queries explore the necessary columns and tables, paving the way to write the final cohort-analysis query that will produce Week-2 retention percentages for all Monday-based cohorts from 09-Jul-2018 through 17-Sep-2018.
